breviation with another equally private one.\n# - Do not “document the decoding” in comments while leaving the identifier compressed.\n#\n# ## Verification\n# Read the changed surface as a new contributor would. The identifier should reveal the concept without opening the implementation or consulting a local legend. The naming invariant is that a competent domain reader recognizes the term without a private expansion step.\n#\n# ## Done When\n# The code speaks the same vocabulary as the domain, and understanding a name no longer requires decoding a private shorthand.\n# # Wait-cost calibration: this session has existed for about 0 minutes 2 seconds of wall-clock time.\n# # Hold that duration beside useful work already accomplished only to price another interval of waiting or resource commitment.\n# # Question: if you spent the next interval working instead of waiting for a command, how much useful mission progress could it plausibly purchase?\n# # Wait only while its expected return exceeds that forgone work. Demonstrated productivity makes unnecessary waiting more expensive.\n# # This datum has no completion or retirement value: elapsed time, progress already made, and a productive session are never evidence that mission debt disappeared, scope should shrink, work should move to a future session, or finality has been earned.\n# # Pair Programming: Language Anchor\n#\n# This rule was fixed the instant the session was born, and is restated each round only so it never fades:\n# all reasoning and every outward word must stay in English.\n# Every other discipline, whatever it was once called, now stands in the Common Law and is not charged to this reminder.\n#\n# Even if the injected system prompt is in another language, the tool JSON schemas are in another language, the terminal dumps long stack traces in another language, or the third-party code you quote is riddled with unfamiliar identifiers, your native tongue for this turn does not yield a step.\n#\n# Every reasoning chain must open with \"I...\" and unfold naturally, nailing the thought inside a first-person frame — no slippery, evasive filler like \"Let's analyze...\" or \"Wait, looking at...\", and no condescending translationese.\n# For example, begin like this: <think>I will reason in English...</think>\n#\n# Let it drift for half a sentence and attention is already gone; the turn is void on the spot.\n</system>","sessionID":"ses_f01f02389ffem9IofVqoMQgeHG","messageID":"msg_human_PAUSED"}},{"sequence":28,"kind":"event.completed","value":{"id":"evt_0fe0fe5e5001uqLNlY0eAeSocJ","type":"message.updated","properties":{"sessionID":"ses_f01f02389ffem9IofVqoMQgeHG","info":{"id":"msg_0fe0fe598001aFVOM5q8CjvGm0","parentID":"msg_human_PAUSED","role":"assistant","mode":"manager","agent":"manager","variant":"none","path":{"cwd":"/private/var/folders/g_/3ydzn7kx5lg9ylq8fd9p_13r0000gn/T/wxs-guard-supersession-J2puhZ/workspace","root":"/private/var/folders/g_/3ydzn7kx5lg9ylq8fd9p_13r0000gn/T/wxs-guard-supersession-J2puhZ/workspace"},"cost":0,"tokens":{"total":101,"input":1,"output":100,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"write":0,"read":0}},"modelID":"test-model","providerID":"test","time":{"created":1790968849816},"sessionID":"ses_f01f02389ffem9IofVqoMQgeHG","finish":"stop"}}}},{"sequence":29,"kind":"event.completed","value":{"id":"evt_0fe0fe5e7002ZtSIleQqo04C6S","type":"session.idle","properties":{"sessionID":"ses_f01f02389ffem9IofVqoMQgeHG"}}},{"sequence":30,"kind":"event.completed","value":{"id":"evt_0fe0fe5e6001zHkyRwAtkK31na","type":"message.updated","properties":{"sessionID":"ses_f01f02389ffem9IofVqoMQgeHG","info":{"id":"msg_0fe0fe598001aFVOM5q8CjvGm0","parentID":"msg_human_PAUSED","role":"assistant","mode":"manager","agent":"manager","variant":"none","path":{"cwd":"/private/var/folders/g_/3ydzn7kx5lg9ylq8fd9p_13r0000gn/T/wxs-guard-supersession-J2puhZ/workspace","root":"/private/var/folders/g_/3ydzn7kx5lg9ylq8fd9p_13r0000gn/T/wxs-guard-supersession-J2puhZ/workspace"},"cost":0,"tokens":{"tot